## 2. Dynamic Business Logic & Derived Status

The status of any physical hardware asset is dynamically calculated on-the-fly using high-performance SQL subqueries matching this precedence hierarchy:

```sql
CASE
  -- 1. Unresolved Damage Report -> Asset is DAMAGED
  WHEN EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM damage_reports dr 
    WHERE dr.asset_id = a.id AND dr.resolution_status = 'Unresolved'
  ) THEN 'damaged'
  
  -- 2. Outstanding Active Allocation -> Asset is ALLOCATED
  WHEN EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM allocations al 
    WHERE al.asset_id = a.id AND al.id NOT IN (SELECT allocation_id FROM returns)
  ) THEN 'allocated'
  
  -- 3. Otherwise -> Asset is IN STOCK
  ELSE 'in_stock'
END AS current_status
```

### Strictly Enforced Backend Rules:
*   **Cannot Allocate Unavailable Asset**: Checked in [allocationController.js](file:///c:/Users/Admin/GENBLAZE/backend/src/controllers/allocationController.js#L21-L36). If an asset is already allocated or has an unresolved damage report, allocation fails with `400 Bad Request`.
*   **Cannot Return Unallocated Asset**: Checked in [returnController.js](file:///c:/Users/Admin/GENBLAZE/backend/src/controllers/returnController.js#L21-L30). Returns must correspond to active, unresolved allocations.
*   **Unique Database Serialization**: Ensured during asset creation in [assetController.js](file:///c:/Users/Admin/GENBLAZE/backend/src/controllers/assetController.js#L143-L162) for serial number and asset tags.
*   **Damage Validation**: Enforced in [damageController.js](file:///c:/Users/Admin/GENBLAZE/backend/src/controllers/damageController.js#L12-L17) requiring descriptions to be $\ge 20$ characters.

